KORVANE HAM-2 WALTERSHOF - GATE INCIDENT NOTE (handwritten, form SAF-1 / paper copy)
Report no. HAM-GI-2024-031. Date: 11.09.2024. Time of event: 14:42 (first wrote 14:24, crossed out, 14:42 is right, checked the barrier log). Written by: K. Aydin, gate guard, late shift.

What happened: Truck of carrier Trans-Wislanka, plate GD 7XK41, driver Zbigniew Kaluza, was reversing out of Lane 2 after a refused entry. The left mirror caught the barrier arm of Gate 2 and snapped it about 1.2 m from the hinge. Driver says the mirror was folded wrong, I say he did not check. Nobody hurt. Barrier arm on the floor, no vehicle damage except the mirror housing cracked.

Reefer on the trailer: unit KCU-0197, display showed +3.8 C, setpoint +2 C (written on the delivery paper). Unit running, plugged at pedestal H-09 while the truck waited. I told Greta because of the reading. She said hold the truck, do not let him go until the display is under +3.0. It took 22 minutes to get there. Truck left gate 15:31.

Damage: barrier arm and motor cover. Estimate from facility, 640 EUR, parts ordered from the supplier Monday. Gate 2 closed for incoming trucks, Gate 1 used, queue max 7 trucks at 15:10, no complaints worth writing down.

Witnesses: Hanneke is not here, so witnesses are S. Brandt (forklift driver, saw the whole thing from bay 3) and the other guard Ilka Moers. Photos: 6 taken with the gate tablet, saved in Tidewalk folder GI-031.

Police not called, no third party damage. Category C I think (no injury, property under 5,000 EUR), Greta to confirm. Reported to Duty Ops at 14:58, 16 minutes after, which is fine, the 15 minute rule is for category B so this is not even needed, but Greta said do it.

Greta signed at 16:05. Copy to Quality (Benedikta) by tomorrow 12:00. Driver asked for a coffee, got one.

Signed: K. Aydin 11.09.24. Seen G. Hohenfeld.
